  "prefLabel": "Cor 305.25 Debarment from Departmental Facilities",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cor 305.25 Debarment from Departmental Facilities. Visitors or others who fail to follow the rules pertaining to NHDOC facilities or areas shall be barred from re-entry thereon by the commissioner, or person in charge of the facility or their agent, by notifying them in person or in writing of the debarment, the reasons therefore, and the duration of the debarment. Persons found to be in violation of the debarment order shall be reported to law enforcement authorities for possible prosecution under the provisions of RSA 635:2, or other appropriate statutes. All debarred persons shall have the right of appeal to the applicable warden, director or designee.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, and #4 at chapter heading for Cor 300) #13154, eff 1-5-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cor100-700.html"
